# Cross-platform & remote Nests

Hatchery must run as a **Hatchery Controller** on Linux, macOS, and Windows, and manage **Local Nests** and/or **Remote Nests** (libvirt/KVM, UTM, Hyper-V). Epic: [#202](https://github.com/dustinestes/Hatchery/issues/202).

**Architecture (locked):** [Controller plane vs Nest plane](../../.hatchery/docs/architecture-nests.md) — one product shell; Nest providers are first-class optional modules. Do not fork into three apps; do not bypass Nest registry/factory (#207 / #206).

## Architecture nouns

| Noun | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **Hatchery Controller** (Controller) | Device where the Hatchery UI runs; responsible for controlling the Nest(s). May have only Remote Nests ([#266](https://github.com/dustinestes/Hatchery/issues/266)). |
| **Nest** | Hypervisor the Controller communicates with to manage guest VMs |
| **Local Nest** | Nest on the same device as the Controller (`location=local`). Nest-local tools (`virsh`, `utmctl`, Hyper-V) apply only here. |
| **Remote Nest** | Nest the Controller reaches across the control plane (`location=remote`). Nest-side hypervisor tools live on the Nest; the Controller needs transport client tools. |

## Two planes

| Plane | Own |
|---|---|
| **Controller** | App runtime, UI, Settings, DB, Library, orchestration, Nest transport client |
| **Nest** | Hypervisor lifecycle via `BaseProvider` (libvirt / UTM / Hyper-V × Local or Remote) |

Controller requirements ≠ Nest-local tool requirements ([#208](https://github.com/dustinestes/Hatchery/issues/208)). New health checks register as **validators** ([#268](https://github.com/dustinestes/Hatchery/issues/268); [validators.md](../../.hatchery/docs/validators.md)) — do not extend a private catch-all loop in `hatchery.py`. Libvirt-only rules stay in the libvirt adapter.

## Distribution north star ([#273](https://github.com/dustinestes/Hatchery/issues/273))

**Long-term consumer install:** OS package managers (apt / brew / winget — and optional PyPI / `pipx` middle) ship **Controller only**. Fresh install → UI with **no Nests**; Nest setup is docs + validators (reachability → transport → Nest hypervisor usability). Do not bake Nest hypervisor packages into the core Controller install.

| Path | Expectation |
|---|---|
| **Consumer** | Package manager → CLI → UI. No git clone. No user-facing gunicorn. |
| **Contributor / tests** | Clone, `uv`, gunicorn (or equivalent) remain valid for development and CI |

Prefer shapes that still work if Hatchery is installed under a system prefix (no repo checkout, no `WorkingDirectory=/path/to/clone`). Checkout-coupled helpers (e.g. v1 `scripts/install-service.sh`) are POC — do not extend them as the product install surface. Ship package formulas **after** Controller is Nest-optional and multi-OS; keep this goal in mind on every install/run/path change.

## Multi-OS CI (required)

PR acceptance runs the **portable** pytest suite on **ubuntu-latest**, **macos-latest**, and **windows-latest** (`.github/workflows/test.yml`). Coverage gate applies on each OS (`pyproject.toml`).

- Do **not** add host-OS-only assumptions that break CI on another runner
- Tests that need a real Nest/hypervisor use `@pytest.mark.hypervisor` and are **excluded** from CI (`-m "not hypervisor"`)
- Mock Nest transport and provider subprocesses in the default suite

```
✅ Pathlib, mocked virsh/ssh, skipif for optional tools (e.g. pwsh)
❌ Hard-code /usr/bin/… or apt-only checks in portable code paths under test
❌ New “integration” tests that require KVM/UTM/Hyper-V without the hypervisor mark
```

## Always ask

```
✅ Does this work on Linux, macOS, and Windows Controllers?
✅ Does this assume a Local Nest only, or also Remote Nest / Controller-only?
✅ Are OS-specific paths (apt, xdg-open, systemd, .desktop) behind a portable helper?
✅ Did you update `.hatchery/docs/providers.md` if Nest/provider capability changed?
✅ Does this go through Nest id → factory (#206/#207), not hard-wired libvirt?
✅ Would this still work if Hatchery were installed via package manager (no git checkout)? (#273)
✅ Does the Controller still start with zero Nests registered?
```

```
❌ Bake apt/dpkg, xdg-open, or systemd as the only path
❌ Hard-wire LibvirtProvider when the call should go through the Nest factory (#206)
❌ Demand Local Nest hypervisor packages on a Controller that only has Remote Nests
❌ Treat Mac/Windows as afterthoughts or permanent sys.platform product shims
❌ Three divergent products instead of modular Nest adapters
❌ New consumer docs that prescribe clone + gunicorn as the primary install path
❌ Extend checkout-coupled install scripts as the long-term product surface (#273)
❌ Require Nest hypervisor tools just to launch the Controller UI
```
